! Dilatancy test case for verification with dilatancy_tests.ipynb
! Problem: 3D planar fault with fluid injection and dilatancy
!
! Run twice:
!   1) With dilatancy T  (this file, filenumber 203)
!   2) With dilatancy F  (change filenumber to 204 and set dilatancy F)
!
! The notebook compares the two runs and verifies the ODE integration.

filenumber 203
problem 3dp

! Grid — 40x40 keeps runtime short while giving enough resolution
imax 40
jmax 40
ds 0.05

! Time stepping
nstep 50
interval 1
tmax 3.0
dtout 0.05

! Rate-and-state friction
! a < b → velocity-weakening (earthquake-prone)
a 0.015
b 0.020
dc 0.0005
f0 0.6
vref 1e-6
muinit 0.55
sigmainit 50.0
velinit 1e-9
backslip T
vpl 0d0

! Pressure diffusion with central injection
pressurediffusion T
injection flowrate
qinj 5e-4
tinj 3.0

! Fluid / pore properties
phi 0.1
beta 5e-8
eta 0.89e-3
kp 1e-15

! Permeability evolution
permev T
kpmin 1e-16
kpmax 1e-13
kT 1e15
kL 1e-3

! Dilatancy — the key parameters under test
dilatancy T
dilatancy_plastic  T
dilatancy_elastic  T
dilatancy_viscous  T
Ld 1.0
eps_d 2e-4
beta_phi 1e-8
eta_s 1e12